-Ray-Occlusion Traversal in Octree is a method for determining shadow ray intersections within a hierarchical voxel (octree) structure by traversing the tree to find the first non-empty leaf or surface [S1, S3, unofficial]. It handles rays starting inside or outside the root voxel by computing entry points via bounding box intersection and stepping through empty space or descending into child nodes [S1, unofficial]. It explicitly manages shadow ray occlusion logic, including specific attenuation factors and boundary precision handling [S1, unofficial].
